# Project Legacy Log

Persistent history of AI-assisted work on `sim_rich_analysis`. Read this at the start of a new
session before proposing changes. Entries are collapsed to high-signal summaries per CLAUDE.md
§7 — verbose debugging narratives are replaced with the retrospective lesson once resolved.

---

## Session 2026-07-29 (a)

**Request:** Add a pinned, multi-line tqdm progress dashboard covering every pipeline stage and
sub-stage, plus a full pytest test suite for every stage/sub-stage.

**Changes:**
- New `progress.py`: `pipeline_bar`/`bar`/`write` helpers. Nesting is by fixed `position=`
  (PIPELINE=0, STAGE=1, STEP=2, capped at 3 depths) — wired into `parsing.py`, `embeddings.py`,
  `distances.py`, `analysis.py`, `run.py`. Milestone `print()`s replaced with `progress.write()`
  so they don't corrupt the pinned bars.
- New `tests/` package: `conftest.py` (synthetic trial-JSON factory, tiny generated images,
  `StubExtractor` faking the CNN) + one `test_<module>.py` per pipeline module + `test_run.py`
  (full synthetic smoke test) + `test_slow_e2e.py` (real-data e2e, opt-in).
- `environment.yml`: added `tqdm`, `pytest`. New `pytest.ini`: registers the `slow` marker,
  `addopts = -m "not slow"` deselects it by default.
- `CLAUDE.md` / `README.md`: documented the new test suite and `progress.py`.

**Trials and errors:** This environment already has real `src_data`/weights present (unusual for
a generic dev box), so `test_slow_e2e.py`'s `skipif` alone would NOT make it a no-op under plain
`pytest` — required `pytest.ini`'s `addopts` to explicitly deselect `slow` by default.

**Retrospective:** Fixed `position=` (not tqdm's auto-assignment) is what keeps a multi-line
dashboard pinned instead of scrolling. Reusable convention: 3 depths (pipeline / stage / step) is
enough; don't nest deeper or fast inner loops just flicker without adding signal.

