## Session 2026-07-29 (b)

**Request:** Compose an educational math/stats/philosophical companion document for the pipeline
(LaTeX, LyX-compilable), matching the structure/style of an existing reference companion PDF
(`mask_discovery_companion.pdf`), delivered as `.tex` + `.lyx` + compiled `.pdf` in a new sibling
`supplamentary/` directory (spelled as the user typed it).

**Changes:** `supplamentary/sim_rich_analysis_companion.{tex,lyx,pdf}`. Content grounded in the
actual original study deck (`SimRich Pres 29.12.25.pdf`, titled "Online Similarity Consciousness")
rather than guessed methodology.

**Trials and errors:**
- Overfull `\hbox`es from long `\texttt` identifiers/inline equations — fixed via `microtype` +
  `lmodern` + `T1` fontenc (plain `T1` alone falls back to bitmap "EC" fonts on this system, which
  breaks `microtype`'s font-expansion) + moving a couple of dense inline formulas to display
  equations.
- `tex2lyx` round-trip (verified by actually re-exporting the `.lyx` back to `.tex` and compiling
  it, not just assuming success) failed twice: (1) a custom `\newtheorem{claim}` collided with
  LyX's own built-in "Claim" AMS-theorem module → duplicate definition; fixed by reusing the
  existing `proposition` environment instead of a bespoke `claim` one. (2) `tex2lyx`'s optional-
  argument parser silently stripped braces inside `\begin{tikzpicture}[...]` style defs and
  mis-parsed the `positioning` library's `right=... of ...` node syntax; fixed by moving the whole
  diagram into a single bracket-argument-free `\newcommand{\pipelinediagram}{...}` in the
  preamble, invoked bare (no brackets) in the body.

**Retrospective:** "LyX-compilable" needs an actual round trip to verify (tex2lyx → lyx --export
latex → pdflatex), not just a successful `pdflatex` run on the hand-written source. Reusable
lesson: any TikZ content destined for LyX conversion belongs in a bracket-free preamble macro —
`tex2lyx`'s TikZ-argument parsing is unreliable for anything beyond the simplest `[key=val]` pairs.

