## Session 2026-07-29 (c)

**Request:** Color-code "best layer" dots by winning layer (with legend); explicitly label which
layer every other RSA figure uses; add a new per-block performance metric (most informative set
of diagrams); generally make every diagram more informative; ensure no legend ever occludes data.

**Changes:**
- `config.py`: `LAYER_COLORS` (colorblind-safe, one per layer).
- `sim_vectors.py`: `build_block_assignment` (per-participant block-membership lookup, mirrors
  `build_human_similarity_vectors`).
- `parsing.py`: `letter_accuracy_by_participant_and_block`.
- `analysis.py`: `best_layer_per_participant` now returns a DataFrame (`pearson_r` +
  `best_layer` columns) instead of a bare Series — needed so callers know *which* layer won, not
  just the score. New `per_participant_correlations_by_block`.
- `plotting.py`: `bar_with_dots`/`bar_with_noise_ceiling` rewritten — `dot_categories_by_level`
  color-coding + legend, `reference_lines` (zero by default, overridable), `bar_label` value
  labels on every bar, per-level N baked into x-tick labels, corrected `xlabel` (was hardcoded and
  wrong: `"Model"`), legend always placed *below* the axes.
- `run.py`: wired 2 new figures (`{condition}_by_block`, `letters_accuracy_by_block`) and added
  `(layer: ...)` to every fixed-layer figure's title.
- Tests extended across `test_sim_vectors.py`, `test_parsing.py`, `test_analysis.py`,
  `test_plotting.py`, `test_run.py`.

**Trials and errors:**
- A standalone (non-pytest) verification script appeared to hang for ~44 minutes; root cause was
  the script never setting `matplotlib.use("Agg")`, so `plt.show()` blocked on an interactive Qt
  backend — unrelated to pipeline code, but wastes real time if repeated.
- Fixing the backend then exposed a *real* bug: a NaN correlation (triggered here by a synthetic
  all-participants-excluded scenario, but also possible in production from a single zero-variance
  participant) crashed matplotlib's categorical string x-axis during `scatter()`
  (`ConversionError`). Fixed with `.dropna()` before every scatter call in both plotting functions;
  regression tests added (`test_bar_with_dots_handles_nan_and_empty_series` and the noise-ceiling
  equivalent).
- Also caught: a module-level `DEFAULT_LAYER_LABEL` constant computed once at `run.py` import
  time — would go stale under `config` monkeypatching (same class of bug as a mutable default
  argument). Moved to a local variable computed fresh inside `_run_condition`.

**Retrospective:** Smoke-testing with a deliberately degenerate synthetic scenario (all
participants excluded) is what surfaced the NaN/matplotlib bug — a happy-path-only smoke test
would have missed it. Reusable lesson: never compute a `config`-derived "constant" at module
import time if `config` might be monkeypatched later (tests, or future runtime reconfiguration);
compute it inside the function that consumes it.

